#X text 1914 686 BUG 1+2 FIX (added 2026-08-21) -- bridge_slicer's live playback trigger arrives here UNTAGGED (first element is the track name itself \, e.g. "vocals 0 0.25 0.5 1 4000 17 1" -- see bridge_slicer.pd's own outlet-0 doc comment) \, so it never matched any selector in the route above and silently fell to the reject outlet (print buffer_manager_unhandled). obj 111 catches it directly off the main inlet \, in parallel with the existing route \, and tags it "play" before forwarding to the matching buffer_manager_stem instance. Also: bare "stop"/"resume" (no track at all -- bridge_slicer sends these as literally just the word \, see performStopNow()/the resume block in slicer_bridge.js) previously fell into a per-stem "route voc drm bss mel" dispatcher that had nothing to match against and dropped them too -- 116/117 fan those out to all 4 stem instances directly instead. The existing "preload" dispatcher (route vocals drums bass melody \, just above this comment) had the same short-code-vs-full-name mismatch as the old play path -- fixed in place by reordering its own argument list to match the full names bridge_slicer actually sends \, so its existing wiring/connections didn't need to change., f 70;
#X obj 1894 337 list trim;
#X obj 1892 424 list trim;
#X obj 1896 516 list trim;
#X obj 1907 627 list trim;
#X text 1914 956 LIST-TRIM FIX (added 2026-08-21) -- confirmed live via buffer_manager_stem_unknown_msg: [list prepend X] does not turn a numbers-only list into a genuine X-selector message -- it stays selector "list" \, with X as merely the first data atom (visible in the console as "list play ..."/"list preload ..." instead of matching route's "play"/"preload" case downstream). [list trim] (already used elsewhere in this codebase\\\, e.g. the read-message builders in buffer_manager_stem.pd) strips that "list" wrapper back off. 119-122 fix the pre-existing preload path (85-88 \, silently broken the same way before this fix -- not something I touched earlier)\\\; 123-126 fix the play path (112-115) added above., f 70;
#X obj 508 1376 list trim;
#X obj 822 1374 list trim;
#X obj 1126 1374 list trim;
#X obj 1438 1372 list trim;
#X text 1914 1129 LIST-TRIM FIX PT.2 (added 2026-08-21) -- the per-stem "route prepare commit stop resume" -> [list prepend <stem>] -> [list prepend prepare] chain (28-30 vocals\\\, 34-36 drums\\\, 40-42 bass\\\, 46-48 melody) has the SAME double list-wrapping problem -- two chained [list prepend]s never produce a genuine "prepare"-selector message\\\, so it would never have matched slot_router.pd's own leading "route prepare commit stop resume" either. 128-131 trim each stem's final output before it reaches outlet 22 (-> slot_router). The commit/stop/resume siblings (31-33/37-39/43-45/49-51) are plain fixed-text message boxes\\\, not [list prepend]\\\, so they were never affected and don't need this., f 70;
#X obj 507 1459 list prepend vocals;
