#X text 1916 1295 SET RELAY (added 2026-08-21) -- route (obj 28/34/40/46) gained a 5th "set" case: buffer_manager_stem.pd's RING-SLOT PLAYBACK SWITCH now emits "set <ringarrayname>" once a ring-buffer compose finishes for that stem \, so the freshly-composed segment can actually be heard instead of always the full \$1-mono buffer from position 0 133-135 (vocals) \, 136-138 (drums) \, 139-141 (bass) \, 142-144 (melody) rebuild a genuine "set <fullstem> <ringarrayname>" selector message the same way the prepare/commit/stop/resume siblings above do (two chained [list prepend]s + [list trim] -- a single [list prepend] never produces a real selector\\\, same fix as LIST-TRIM FIX PT.2 just above) \, then feed the shared outlet 22 toward slot_router.pd \, which has its own matching "set" case (added 2026-08-21) to route it on to the right stem., f 70;
